After refactoring, make sure the code still passes the tests.  Run the tests using this command:
```sh
crisp_run_tests.sh
```
This will exit zero if the tests passed and nonzero if they failed.  In either case, it returns the test logs as the body.

Note: when the C codebase includes its own tests, this always uses the original version of those tests.  You MUST NOT edit any test code outside `crisp_tests/` or the original C code, and doing so will have no effect on any pre-existing tests run by this command.  Instead, you must ensure that your edits to the codebase preserve ALL externally-visible behavior that's exercised by the tests.  (This does not apply to the differential tests in `crisp_tests/`; for those, this command always runs the current version of the test code.)
